930","position":"1795119112545597578-aae9c896-8052-4df8-8c66-1443b6ad029b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a31ca54a87725662d1b9dffe4aa93d364807b68bbd71fa2dda78eccdd9323c3c","event_uuid":"9a332736-2035-4a48-8fff-33aa73272586","position":{"commit_sha":"79a52b0600ae4315a3e8ba7d42442cb90cb88ff8","position":"1795119623116035883-9a332736-2035-4a48-8fff-33aa73272586"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The 28 op-cert tests are moved into `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` by the almondy-columned-iguanodon change (5888f4941be, pending Gerrit). That change also adds the non-gating `icacls` step to the Windows sweep, which prints the ACL of a fresh key's folder, the key, and a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory.","timestamp":1795053193354557121},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"First hypothesis supported by the sweep's `icacls` step (run 44456347985, job 135332660982): a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory on the Windows runner (Python 3.13) carries exactly `NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(F)`, `BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(F)`, `OWNER RIGHTS:(OI)(CI)(F)`, and the OWNER RIGHTS entry is inheritable, so the key copy written into it inherits the ACE Win32-OpenSSH rejects. By contrast a key minted by `ssh-keygen` gets explicit Administrators / SYSTEM / owner-user entries. Not yet checked: the key copy's own ACL (the step does not write one), which would confirm the inheritance directly.","timestamp":1795066881582937119},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision (2026-11-19 PST): option (1). On Windows only, rebar writes an owner-only DACL on the temporary op-cert key copy it creates for signing, so that Win32-OpenSSH accepts it and op-cert signing works on Windows. Principle: anyone can sign, so no platform is excluded. This does not change the nymph decision, which covers the persistent key file (rely on the default ACL). The 28 tests in `openssh-key-acl.args` return to the Windows sweep.","timestamp":1795109818495387399},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Source of the OWNER RIGHTS ACE confirmed (AC1). Throwaway diag branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl` (never merged), `sweep (windows)` run 44581143998, job 135761807560, Python 3.13 on windows-latest, running as runnervmm7ud1\\runneradmin:\n- The runner temp folder `C:\\Users\\RUNNER~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp` carries SYSTEM, Administrators and runneradmin, all (OI)(CI)(F). No OWNER RIGHTS entry, so the second hypothesis (temp folder ACL) is refuted.\n- A fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rebar-opcert-\")` dir carries exactly SYSTEM, Administrators and OWNER RIGHTS, all (OI)(CI)(F). The user's own entry is gone, which matches Python 3.13's `os.mkdir(mode=0o700)` on Windows replacing the DACL.\n- The key copy written into it by `keyprov._write_copy` carries exactly SYSTEM:(F), Administrators:(F), OWNER RIGHTS:(F), so it takes its ACL from that dir.\n- `ssh-keygen -y -P \"\" -f <copy>` exits 255 with \"Bad permissions. Try removing permissions for user: \\\\OWNER RIGHTS (S-1-3-4)\".\nAll 28 tests in `openssh-key-acl.args` fail or error with that same OpcertKeyError in the same run.\n\nConclusion: the ACE comes from the DACL that `tempfile.mkdtemp` (Python 3.13 `os.mkdir(mode=0o700)`) writes on the runtime dir. The copy takes that DACL when it is created.","timestamp":1795110665831666556},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress. The fix is committed locally (Change-Id I1d214d73df17cafc33bc346ebc3da28403bd0a98) and `make verify` is running.\n\nPre-merge Windows evidence comes from the throwaway branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl`, which runs the 28 tests plus the new test file on windows-latest.\n- Run 44590213544 (fix applied): op-cert signing now composes and signs on Windows. 34 passed, 1 skipped (the POSIX-only test), 3 failed. All 6 new tests pass, including the real-ACL test `test_windows_copy_acl_names_only_the_current_user`.\n- The 3 failures are separate defects. The ACL fix exposed them, because compose_signer used to fail first:\n  - `test_completion_pass_spawn_ceiling` and `test_completion_fail_spawn_ceiling` fail because `project_ensures._PROJECTS_REL_PATH` uses `os.path.join` inside a git revision path (`tickets:.bridge_state\\projects.json`). The lookup misses on Windows, so the seed rewrites projects.json on every sweep, which adds spawns. Filed as undamaging-ashamed-wasp. With that one-line fix applied, run 44591481319 shows both passing.\n  - `test_signer_test_modules_leave_no_key_copy_in_the_temp_dir` fails because its nested run's TMPDIR and basetemp sit under a deep tmp_path, and git hits \"Filename too long\" (MAX_PATH). Filed as flowered-nonvalued-mink (test-only fix). Run 44592408164 is testing it.\n\nOrdering: wasp and mink land on main BEFORE this change, so that deleting `openssh-key-acl.args` here does not turn the main sweep red. AC2 is checked on main after all 3 land.\n\nPortability: the new code runs only where os.name == \"nt\". It uses subprocess with an argument list, a timeout and lenient decoding, and adds no POSIX-only API.","timestamp":1795114453516356371},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pre-merge Windows check of the full stack passed. The stack is undamaging-ashamed-wasp \u2192 flowered-nonvalued-mink \u2192 inaccurate-genetic-asianlion \u2192 this change. Throwaway branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl` at 18cdfe2ff80, `sweep (windows)` run 44606991897, job 135853215223, conclusion success. The 28 former `openssh-key-acl.args` tests, plus the new tests of all 4 tickets: 44 passed, 1 skipped (the POSIX-only test). inaccurate-genetic-asianlion is the third defect found here: on Windows, op-cert job workspaces leaked because `discard`'s rmtree cannot delete git's read-only objects. That leak was the last cause of the nested leak test failing. The stack lands in that order so the main sweep stays green. `make verify` is running on the stack tip.","timestamp":1795119623116035883}],"created_at":1795051614823743457,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"69897b2e-9eb7-471e-8d54-ec1cf773030b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"44b2-e70e-2b9f-4d2a"},{"link_uuid":"4785e4bc-fbed-4221-a210-f8a4570e8a2a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"47d8-baf8-2348-45c9"},{"link_uuid":"17bb7c3c-a887-466e-b93c-519698b19f1c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"6f5a-b6e4-327e-46b4"},{"link_uuid":"4315c265-6199-495b-9bf7-e4df0f21a592","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d4f1-da58-0748-4e1a"},{"link_uuid":"c31c45b3-f743-4124-ab78-244c9377499d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"387c-d59c-7854-40b2"},{"link_uuid":"aae9c896-8052-4df8-8c66-1443b6ad029b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6727-7d54-9f76-40bd"}],"description":"## Observation\nIn the scheduled Windows sweep at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16), `tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py::test_compose_still_works_after_pop` failed in `rebar.opcert_service.keyprov.compose_signer`: `OpcertKeyError: the op-cert key is malformed, encrypted (passphrase-protected), or otherwise unusable: Bad permissions. Try removing permissions for user: \\OWNER RIGHTS (S-1-3-4) on file C:/Users/RUNN...`. That test supplies the key inline, so it never reaches rebar's own mode check; the refusal comes from `ssh-keygen -y` (`src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py:137-162`), which validates the copy `compose_signer` writes into a `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory (`keyprov.py:73`).\n\nWin32-OpenSSH's key permission check accepts only the file owner, SYSTEM and Administrators. The copy's ACL carries an OWNER RIGHTS ACE. Every `compose_signer` path writes the same kind of copy, so once rebar's POSIX mode check is skipped on Windows (almondy-columned-iguanodon) the 30 op-cert tests in `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` are expected to stop here.\n\n## Hypotheses\nResolved by the diag run (see comments): the ACE comes from `tempfile.mkdtemp`'s DACL, not the temp folder.\n\n## Note on policy\nMaking the copy acceptable to OpenSSH means writing an owner-only DACL on it. On cloistered-decomposed-nymph (2026-11-18) the operator chose option (3), relying on the default ACL, and rejected option (1), an owner-only DACL check plus a protected DACL on key copies. Resolved 2026-11-19 (see comments): option (1) on this ticket reverses that rejection for the temporary copy only, on Windows only; the persistent key file still relies on the default ACL.\n\n## Context / Problem\nOp-cert signing cannot compose on Windows: Win32-OpenSSH refuses the temporary key copy that `compose_signer` writes, because the copy carries an OWNER RIGHTS ACE. The diag run recorded in the comments (run 44581143998) shows the ACE comes from the DACL Python 3.13's `tempfile.mkdtemp` writes on the runtime dir (SYSTEM, Administrators, OWNER RIGHTS; no user entry), and the copy takes that DACL. Operator decision (2026-11-19, option 1, recorded in the comments): on Windows only, rebar writes an owner-only DACL on that temporary copy; POSIX behaviour and the persistent key file's handling (cloistered-decomposed-nymph option 3, default ACL) are unchanged. The 28 tests in `openssh-key-acl.args` (not 30) fail for this reason.\n\n## Approach\nIn `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py`, `compose_signer` gains one Windows-only step, inside its existing cleanup `try`, BEFORE `_write_copy` runs: a new helper `_restrict_dir_to_owner(runtime_dir)` gives the runtime dir an owner-only DACL, so the copy is created under it and is never readable by anyone else at any point. The branch is selected by the module's existing `_POSIX_MODE_BITS` switch (False only where `os.name == \"nt\"`), so POSIX hosts run exactly today's code.\n- The helper reads the current user's SID with `whoami /user /fo csv /nh` (parsed with the stdlib `csv` module), then runs `icacls <dir> /inheritance:r /grant:r *<SID>:(OI)(CI)F`, then ONE `icacls <dir> /remove:g` call listing OWNER RIGHTS (`*S-1-3-4`), SYSTEM (`*S-1-5-18`) and Administrators (`*S-1-5-32-544`), skipping any of those that equals the current user's SID. Granting before removing means the user never loses access to the dir.\n- Mechanism choice: `icacls` and `whoami` ship with every supported Windows, so no dependency is added; the repo already runs `icacls` in the sweep's ACL probe step, though only to print ACLs, so the ACL-changing flags and the `whoami` CSV format are new uses here and are proven on a real Windows runner before merge (see Testing). Rejected: building the DACL in-process via the Win32 API over `ctypes`, which needs hand-written structure and handle management with no repo precedent. Tools are launched by bare name, as the module already launches `ssh-keygen`. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n- Each `whoami`/`icacls` call runs with a fixed 60-second subprocess timeout (a constant, not configurable); output is captured as bytes and decoded with `errors=\"replace\"`, since the SID itself is ASCII and only the user-name column can carry non-ASCII text, so a non-ASCII account name cannot raise a decode error.\n- Failure disposition: any failure (tool missing, timeout, non-zero exit, unparseable `whoami` output) raises `OpcertKeyError` with a message beginning `cannot restrict the op-cert key copy` (or naming the SID read) so it is distinguishable from the existing key-content rejections. It is fatal and not retried: `compose_signer` runs once per process start. In the opcert service (`app.py` lifespan) it runs before any queue, worker or network exists; in `rebar-mcp` it runs after the store-sweep and idle-sync daemon threads start, and the error leaves `main()` and ends the process. Either way an operator fixes the host and restarts. The existing `except BaseException` removes the runtime dir, so no copy is stranded.\n- Portability: the new code runs only on Windows and uses `subprocess.run` with an argument list and `os.path` paths; no POSIX-only API, fd, signal or path-separator assumption.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py` \u2014 the Windows-only owner-only DACL step and its helper; module comment updated.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_key_copy_windows_acl.py` (new) \u2014 the tests below.\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` \u2014 deleted, so the 28 tests run on Windows again.\n- `.github/workflows/test.yml` \u2014 drop the `'@.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args'` argument from the sweep command (`tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` keeps the files and the command in step), and update the ACL probe step's comment: it prints a plain `mkdtemp` dir (still OWNER RIGHTS) to show why rebar restricts its runtime dir, and the persistent key's default ACL. The step's name, and so its `mechanism-ok` key, is unchanged.\n- `docs/manifest-signing.md` \u2014 state that on Windows rebar gives its temporary signing copy an owner-only ACL, while the persistent key still relies on the default ACL.\n\n## Testing\n- Windows-capability-guarded (skipped unless `os.name == \"nt\"`): `compose_signer` on a freshly generated Ed25519 key succeeds, and `icacls` on the returned `signer.key_path` (which exists until `cleanup()`) lists the current user and none of OWNER RIGHTS, SYSTEM or Administrators.\n- Portable (all platforms; `_POSIX_MODE_BITS` forced False; `tempfile.tempdir` pointed at an empty per-test dir; `keyprov.subprocess.run` replaced by a fake that answers `whoami`/`icacls` by `argv[0]` and passes `ssh-keygen` to the real `run`): the `whoami`, grant and remove calls happen in that order and all before the copy is written; every call carries the timeout; the remove list skips the current user's SID; a non-zero `icacls` exit, a timeout, a missing tool, or unparseable `whoami` output raises `OpcertKeyError` and leaves no `rebar-opcert-*` dir behind; `whoami` output with a non-ASCII user name still yields the SID.\n- Portable: with `_POSIX_MODE_BITS` True (POSIX) neither `whoami` nor `icacls` is called.\n- Before merge: a `sweep (windows)` run on a throwaway GitHub branch carrying the fix runs the 28 tests. After merge: a `sweep (windows)` run on main with the deselect file gone, checked at the job level; \"the tests in `openssh-key-acl.args`\" means the 28 node ids that file lists at `91322a91e9e`, and the evidence comment names each one's result in that run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The source of the OWNER RIGHTS ACE is identified from the sweep's `icacls` output and recorded here.\n- [ ] Either op-cert signing composes and signs on a Windows runner (the tests in `openssh-key-acl.args` pass in a `sweep (windows)` run on main), or the operator's decision to leave it unsupported is recorded and the tests skip on Windows with that reason.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py","reason":"Windows-only owner-only DACL on the runtime dir before the key copy is written"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_key_copy_windows_acl.py","reason":"new Windows-guarded and portable tests"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args","reason":"deleted so the 28 op-cert tests run on Windows again"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"drop the deleted argfile from the Windows sweep command"},{"path":"docs/manifest-signing.md","reason":"document the temporary copy's owner-only ACL on Windows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","387c-d59c-7854-40b2"],["depends_on","6f5a-b6e4-327e-46b4"],["depends_on","d4f1-da58-0748-4e1a"],["relates_to","47d8-baf8-2348-45c9"],["relates_to","6727-7d54-9f76-40bd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a15a6b82-e6e2-41fe-943d-60316d1e4f00","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability","signing"],"ticket_id":"977f-11fe-1dcb-4b7d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: Win32-OpenSSH rejects the op-cert key copy (OWNER RIGHTS ACE), so signing cannot run on Windows","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5a4309ba-67ab-46cc-8326-ae87c4b952f6","018abd5b-d89f-4ab0-87b5-4e35ae011c5c","88499f0f-8e7d-4a26-b759-2dfdb4d223d9","97358283-f2b3-48af-821f-1a63c1995265","ac17bfed-8b14-4ccf-95b5-6b5d11168995","e6a5b38c-5708-4f55-9b76-1480188bbd00","a35bc60d-9552-4658-9ff9-24f6e79b5261","7ecbd246-08f6-472e-b72a-66f42e0551a3","77f4e6c9-53e3-49ad-80c6-109a28e81a2b","a15a6b82-e6e2-41fe-943d-60316d1e4f00","befb885b-c7c9-40ea-a082-98c2584142cf","50706b56-cc7c-446b-a292-42d691e272cc","17bb7c3c-a887-466e-b93c-519698b19f1c","4315c265-6199-495b-9bf7-e4df0f21a592","c31c45b3-f743-4124-ab78-244c9377499d","aae9c896-8052-4df8-8c66-1443b6ad029b","9a332736-2035-4a48-8fff-33aa73272586"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timest